node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.oold-schema/
site/

# Schemas copied to their published paths (docs/<module>/<version>/) so the site serves
# them and the conformance IRIs resolve. Byte-identical to schemas/, regenerated by
# scripts/build_docs.py before every build and every deploy, so committing them would
# only mean reviewing every schema change twice.
docs/*/[0-9]*/
docs/mappings/**/*.sssom.tsv

# The SSSOM sets: a row is the schema's own mapping metadata transposed into columns, so
# committing them would put a mechanical restatement in every review beside the change it
# restates. The build writes them before anything reads them.
generated/mappings/

# Ontology snapshots fetched from ontologies.lock.json. Pinned and hash-verified, not
# carried: they belong to other projects and nothing in the build reads them, since the
# labels they supply are committed.
.ontologies/
